 ### Rules
 
 - `other` is **always required** — it is the fallback for every language.
-- `#` is the count placeholder inside a plural/selectordinal branch — do not repeat the variable name there.
+- **Write `{count, number}` as the count placeholder, not `#`.** ICU `#` is implemented only on the ICU-JSON format *and* only from `@inlang/paraglide-js` **2.27.0** onward. On the PO format (this skill's default) it is unformatted at **every** 2.x version, and on ICU-JSON at **2.26.x and below** — `1234567` renders as `1234567` in every locale instead of `1,234,567` / `1 234 567` / `1.234.567`. Bare `{count}` inside a branch is unformatted everywhere, by design. **`{count, number}`** (and `{n, number}` for selectordinal) is the one form that is locale-aware on both formats at every version `@inlang/paraglide-js@^2` can resolve to, so write that. Where `#` is unimplemented, ICU-JSON warns once per build (`The formatter "icu:pound" is unknown and will be ignored`) and **PO is silent**.
+- `offset:` in a plural body follows the same split — honoured on ICU-JSON from **2.27.0** (`{count, plural, offset:1 …}` with `count = 1234567` renders `1,234,566`), and **parsed then dropped, with no warning, on PO at every version and on ICU-JSON below 2.27.0**. Do not emit it unless the project is ICU-JSON and pinned at `>= 2.27.0`.
 - CLDR categories: `zero`, `one`, `two`, `few`, `many`, `other` — not `singular` / `plural`. English cardinals need only `one` + `other`.
 - Ordinal categories differ from cardinal — English ordinals use `one` (1st, 21st), `two` (2nd, 22nd), `few` (3rd, 23rd), `other` (4th+).
 - Keep all branches in **one** message body — never split them into separate entries.
